IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rta-driving-offences`
IMPORT `rta-forfeiture-accidents`
IMPORT `rta-speeding`
IMPORT `rta-demerit-points`
IMPORT `rta-seat`

-- Road Traffic Act 1961 -- the driver's questions (rta-seat.l4), worked cases.
--
-- Every fixture and every expected value is copied from the existing, hand-checked case files
-- (rta-cases-driving-offences.l4, rta-cases-forfeiture-accidents.l4, rta-cases-speeding.l4, rta-cases-demerit-points.l4).
-- None is new. The one exception in form is the minimum term: the existing cases assert its two parts (the (a)/(b) minimum
-- and the (c)/(d) minimum) separately, and the fixtures used here are ones where one part is 0, so the total is the other.
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.

§ `Fixtures`

`a sober first-time dangerous driver who harms no one` MEANS Driver WITH
    `manner` IS `dangerous`
    `harm` IS `no harm`
    `is a repeat offender` IS FALSE
    `was also convicted of drink-driving or refusing a breath test` IS FALSE
    `earlier specified offences` IS 0

`a drunk dangerous driver with two earlier drink convictions, no harm` MEANS Driver WITH
    `manner` IS `dangerous`
    `harm` IS `no harm`
    `is a repeat offender` IS FALSE
    `was also convicted of drink-driving or refusing a breath test` IS TRUE
    `earlier specified offences` IS 2

`a sober first-time dangerous driver who kills` MEANS Driver WITH
    `manner` IS `dangerous`
    `harm` IS `death`
    `is a repeat offender` IS FALSE
    `was also convicted of drink-driving or refusing a breath test` IS FALSE
    `earlier specified offences` IS 0

`a sober repeat dangerous driver who kills` MEANS Driver WITH
    `manner` IS `dangerous`
    `harm` IS `death`
    `is a repeat offender` IS TRUE
    `was also convicted of drink-driving or refusing a breath test` IS FALSE
    `earlier specified offences` IS 0

`a drunk first-time dangerous driver who kills` MEANS Driver WITH
    `manner` IS `dangerous`
    `harm` IS `death`
    `is a repeat offender` IS FALSE
    `was also convicted of drink-driving or refusing a breath test` IS TRUE
    `earlier specified offences` IS 0

`texting while moving` MEANS PhoneUse WITH
    `held in the hand` IS TRUE
    `operated a function` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle was in motion` IS TRUE
    `a wearable worn as intended` IS FALSE

`texting at a red light` MEANS PhoneUse WITH
    `held in the hand` IS TRUE
    `operated a function` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle was in motion` IS FALSE
    `a wearable worn as intended` IS FALSE

`a driver with 0 earlier drink convictions` MEANS DrinkRecord WITH
    `earlier drink-driving convictions` IS 0

`a driver with 1 earlier drink convictions` MEANS DrinkRecord WITH
    `earlier drink-driving convictions` IS 1

`a driver with 2 earlier drink convictions` MEANS DrinkRecord WITH
    `earlier drink-driving convictions` IS 2

`a drunk friend who kills in a borrowed car` MEANS ForfeitureCase WITH
    `harm` IS "death"
    `is a serious or serious repeat offender` IS TRUE
    `dangerous rather than careless` IS TRUE
    `the offender is not the owner` IS TRUE
    `used without the owner's consent` IS FALSE
    `the court has other good reasons` IS FALSE

`a drunk joyrider who kills in a stolen car` MEANS ForfeitureCase WITH
    `harm` IS "death"
    `is a serious or serious repeat offender` IS TRUE
    `dangerous rather than careless` IS TRUE
    `the offender is not the owner` IS TRUE
    `used without the owner's consent` IS TRUE
    `the court has other good reasons` IS FALSE

`a sober owner who kills, with good reasons shown` MEANS ForfeitureCase WITH
    `harm` IS "death"
    `is a serious or serious repeat offender` IS FALSE
    `dangerous rather than careless` IS TRUE
    `the offender is not the owner` IS FALSE
    `used without the owner's consent` IS FALSE
    `the court has other good reasons` IS TRUE

`a driver who scraped a parked car, left a note, and was contacted` MEANS Accident WITH
    `damage or injury resulted` IS TRUE
    `stopped` IS TRUE
    `gave particulars to a person at the scene` IS FALSE
    `someone with reasonable grounds was at the scene` IS FALSE
    `took reasonable steps to inform the owner` IS TRUE
    `the owner contacted the driver` IS TRUE
    `reported to the police within 24 hours` IS FALSE

`a driver who left a note, was not contacted, and did not report` MEANS Accident WITH
    `damage or injury resulted` IS TRUE
    `stopped` IS TRUE
    `gave particulars to a person at the scene` IS FALSE
    `someone with reasonable grounds was at the scene` IS FALSE
    `took reasonable steps to inform the owner` IS TRUE
    `the owner contacted the driver` IS FALSE
    `reported to the police within 24 hours` IS FALSE

`a driver who left a note, was not contacted, and reported` MEANS Accident WITH
    `damage or injury resulted` IS TRUE
    `stopped` IS TRUE
    `gave particulars to a person at the scene` IS FALSE
    `someone with reasonable grounds was at the scene` IS FALSE
    `took reasonable steps to inform the owner` IS TRUE
    `the owner contacted the driver` IS FALSE
    `reported to the police within 24 hours` IS TRUE

`a driver who drove off` MEANS Accident WITH
    `damage or injury resulted` IS TRUE
    `stopped` IS FALSE
    `gave particulars to a person at the scene` IS FALSE
    `someone with reasonable grounds was at the scene` IS TRUE
    `took reasonable steps to inform the owner` IS FALSE
    `the owner contacted the driver` IS FALSE
    `reported to the police within 24 hours` IS FALSE

`Jun Hao, a clean record` MEANS RiderRecord WITH
    `the limit in force` IS 90
    `the speed recorded` IS 115
    `points already in 24 months` IS 0
    `points already in 12 months` IS 0
    `earlier suspended or liable` IS FALSE
    `clean for 24 months since` IS FALSE
    `earlier speeding conviction` IS FALSE

`Jun Hao, 16 points already` MEANS RiderRecord WITH
    `the limit in force` IS 90
    `the speed recorded` IS 115
    `points already in 24 months` IS 16
    `points already in 12 months` IS 10
    `earlier suspended or liable` IS FALSE
    `clean for 24 months since` IS FALSE
    `earlier speeding conviction` IS FALSE

`Jun Hao, suspended before` MEANS RiderRecord WITH
    `the limit in force` IS 90
    `the speed recorded` IS 115
    `points already in 24 months` IS 4
    `points already in 12 months` IS 4
    `earlier suspended or liable` IS TRUE
    `clean for 24 months since` IS FALSE
    `earlier speeding conviction` IS FALSE

`Jun Hao, suspended long ago` MEANS RiderRecord WITH
    `the limit in force` IS 90
    `the speed recorded` IS 115
    `points already in 24 months` IS 4
    `points already in 12 months` IS 4
    `earlier suspended or liable` IS TRUE
    `clean for 24 months since` IS TRUE
    `earlier speeding conviction` IS FALSE

§ `Do I need a licence`

#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be jailed for driving without a licence, in months` FALSE EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be jailed for driving without a licence, in months` TRUE EQUALS 72

§ `If I drive dangerously or carelessly`

#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be jailed for my driving, in months` `a sober first-time dangerous driver who harms no one` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be jailed for my driving, in months` `a sober first-time dangerous driver who kills` EQUALS 96
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be jailed for my driving, in months` `a drunk first-time dangerous driver who kills` EQUALS 120

#ASSERT `What is the shortest term I must serve for my driving, in months` `a sober first-time dangerous driver who kills` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the shortest term I must serve for my driving, in months` `a sober repeat dangerous driver who kills` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `What is the shortest term I must serve for my driving, in months` `a drunk first-time dangerous driver who kills` EQUALS 12

#ASSERT `For how many years at least must I be disqualified for my driving` `a sober first-time dangerous driver who kills` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `For how many years at least must I be disqualified for my driving` `a sober repeat dangerous driver who kills` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `For how many years at least must I be disqualified for my driving` `a drunk first-time dangerous driver who kills` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `For how many years at least must I be disqualified for my driving` `a drunk dangerous driver with two earlier drink convictions, no harm` EQUALS 999

§ `My phone`

#ASSERT `Am I committing the phone offence` `texting while moving`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I committing the phone offence` `texting at a red light`

§ `If I drink and drive`

#ASSERT `What is the least I can be fined for drink-driving` `a driver with 0 earlier drink convictions` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `What is the least I can be fined for drink-driving` `a driver with 1 earlier drink convictions` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT NOT `Must I go to prison for drink-driving` `a driver with 0 earlier drink convictions`
#ASSERT `Must I go to prison for drink-driving` `a driver with 1 earlier drink convictions`
#ASSERT `For how many years at least must I be disqualified for drink-driving` `a driver with 0 earlier drink convictions` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `For how many years at least must I be disqualified for drink-driving` `a driver with 2 earlier drink convictions` EQUALS 999
#ASSERT `Does my earlier conviction count towards a tripled punishment` `dangerous driving with no harm, before the 2025 amendments`
#ASSERT NOT `Does my earlier conviction count towards a tripled punishment` `dangerous driving with no harm, after the 2025 amendments`

§ `Can I lose the car`

#ASSERT `Must the car I drove be forfeited` `a drunk friend who kills in a borrowed car`
#ASSERT NOT `Must the car I drove be forfeited` `a drunk joyrider who kills in a stolen car`
#ASSERT NOT `Must the car I drove be forfeited` `a sober owner who kills, with good reasons shown`

§ `After an accident`

#ASSERT NOT `Must I report the accident to the police` `a driver who scraped a parked car, left a note, and was contacted`
#ASSERT `Must I report the accident to the police` `a driver who left a note, was not contacted, and did not report`
#ASSERT `Have I broken the duties after an accident` `a driver who left a note, was not contacted, and did not report`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I broken the duties after an accident` `a driver who left a note, was not contacted, and reported`
#ASSERT `Have I broken the duties after an accident` `a driver who drove off`

§ `If I am caught speeding`

#ASSERT `Am I speeding` 90 115
#ASSERT NOT `Am I speeding` 90 90
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for speeding` TRUE EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound my speeding` TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `How many demerit points do I get for speeding` 25 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `How many demerit points do I get for speeding` 20 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `How many demerit points do I get for speeding` 51 EQUALS 24

§ `My licence`

#ASSERT NOT `Can my licence be suspended for demerit points` `Jun Hao, a clean record`
#ASSERT `Can my licence be suspended for demerit points` `Jun Hao, 16 points already`
#ASSERT `Can my licence be suspended for demerit points` `Jun Hao, suspended before`
#ASSERT NOT `Can my licence be suspended for demerit points` `Jun Hao, suspended long ago`
#ASSERT `How many more points can I get before my licence can be suspended` `Jun Hao, a clean record` EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `How many more points can I get before my licence can be suspended` `Jun Hao, suspended long ago` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `Must I be offered the safe-driving course` 8 8 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must I be offered the safe-driving course` 8 8 FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my licence be revoked because I am a new driver` 200 13 13
#ASSERT NOT `Can my licence be revoked because I am a new driver` 400 13 13
